1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,680
Ava: If a GPU kernel is already tuned, where can more speed come from?
Ava：GPU 内核已经调优了，还能从哪里提速？

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:09,278
That sounds like trying to squeeze water from a dry sponge.
这听起来像是要从干海绵里挤水。

3
00:00:09,278 --> 00:00:11,624
Brian: Surprisingly, from the compiler.
Brian：没想到吧，还能从编译器入手。

4
00:00:11,624 --> 00:00:16,904
This article shows how Helion searches settings below the kernel itself.
这篇文章介绍了 Helion 如何搜索内核本身之外的配置。

5
00:00:16,904 --> 00:00:21,580
On an already tuned kernel, that produced measurable gains.
即使内核已经调优，也取得了可测量的性能提升。

6
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,716
Ava: Okay, let's start with Helion.
Ava：好，那先说说 Helion。

7
00:00:23,716 --> 00:00:28,338
What's already been tuned before the compiler gets its turn?
轮到编译器之前，哪些地方已经调优了？

8
00:00:28,338 --> 00:00:33,610
Brian: Helion lets developers write GPU kernels in PyTorch-native Python.
Brian：Helion 让开发者用 PyTorch 原生 Python 编写 GPU 内核。

9
00:00:33,610 --> 00:00:39,281
A kernel is a program for work on the graphics processing unit, or GPU.
内核是在图形处理器（GPU）上执行任务的程序。

10
00:00:39,281 --> 00:00:43,784
Helion's autotuner tries many ways to run that work.
Helion 的自动调优器会尝试多种执行方式。

11
00:00:43,784 --> 00:00:48,766
Ava: And these weren't weak examples picked to make a speedup look impressive?
Ava：这些例子不是故意挑的弱基线，好让提速显得惊人吧？

12
00:00:48,766 --> 00:00:53,004
Brian: Right. The article starts from Helion's pretuned kernels.
Brian：没错。文章以 Helion 预先调优的内核为起点。

13
00:00:53,004 --> 00:01:02,744
There are roughly twenty-seven, covering work such as quantization, normalization, grouped matrix multiplication, and model decode.
大约有 27 个，涵盖量化、归一化、分组矩阵乘法和模型解码等任务。

14
00:01:02,744 --> 00:01:06,588
Their kernel configurations were tuned offline.
这些内核的配置已经离线调优。

15
00:01:06,588 --> 00:01:11,114
Ava: So someone running one of those kernels doesn't wait for a search?
Ava：所以运行这些内核时，不用再等它搜索？

16
00:01:11,114 --> 00:01:17,414
Brian: Exactly. Each ships with an ahead-of-time configuration for its target architecture.
Brian：对。每个内核都附带针对目标架构预先确定的配置。

17
00:01:17,414 --> 00:01:20,789
Helion selects that configuration at runtime.
Helion 会在运行时选用该配置。

18
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:27,064
The user gets the result of earlier tuning without paying the search cost then.
用户能享受先前调优的成果，当时无需承担搜索开销。

19
00:01:27,064 --> 00:01:33,630
Ava: Good baseline. Now, what does Helion's usual autotuner actually change?
Ava：基线不错。Helion 通常的自动调优器会调整什么？

20
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:39,589
Brian: Think of a large job split into tiles, like dividing a floor into sections to clean.
Brian：想象把一项大任务分成许多块，就像把地板分区清扫。

21
00:01:39,589 --> 00:01:45,260
Helion decides each tile's size and how the GPU's thread groups work on it.
Helion 决定每块的大小，以及 GPU 线程组如何处理它。

22
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:50,770
Ava: So the developer marks the work as tiled, and Helion picks the details?
Ava：开发者只需指定分块处理，细节交给 Helion 选？

23
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:58,429
Brian: Yes. It can search block sizes, warp counts, pipeline stages, memory indexing, and more.
Brian：对。它可以搜索块大小、warp 数量、流水线阶段数、内存索引方式等。

24
00:01:58,429 --> 00:02:01,301
A warp is a group of GPU threads.
warp 是一组 GPU 线程。

25
00:02:01,301 --> 00:02:06,960
Helion compiles candidates, times them, and keeps the winner.
Helion 编译各个候选方案、测量耗时，然后选出最快的。

26
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,566
Ava: Where does the new layer begin?
Ava：新的调优层从哪里开始？

27
00:02:09,566 --> 00:02:18,620
Brian: After Helion lowers the kernel through TorchInductor to Triton, the winning candidate reaches ptxas, NVIDIA's PTX assembler.
Brian：Helion 通过 TorchInductor 将内核降级到 Triton 后，胜出的候选方案会交给 NVIDIA 的 PTX 汇编器 ptxas。

28
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:23,000
It turns that lower-level program into machine instructions.
它把这个更底层的程序转换成机器指令。

29
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,220
Traditionally, its controls stayed at their defaults.
过去，它的控制选项通常保持默认值。

30
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:32,202
Ava: What kind of controls are we talking about? More tile sizes?
Ava：这些选项控制什么？也是块大小吗？

31
00:02:32,202 --> 00:02:40,159
Brian: No. These affect choices such as register allocation, instruction scheduling, and code-generation heuristics.
Brian：不是。它们影响寄存器分配、指令调度和代码生成启发式策略等选择。

32
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:42,934
Registers are fast storage on the GPU.
寄存器是 GPU 上的高速存储。

33
00:02:42,934 --> 00:02:50,000
The kernel's tile can stay the same while the compiler handles its instructions differently.
内核的分块可以不变，但编译器处理其指令的方式会改变。

34
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,870
Ava: That sounds hard to set by hand.
Ava：听起来很难手动设置。

35
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:53,340
Brian: It is.
Brian：确实。

36
00:02:53,340 --> 00:03:00,159
One register decision can change occupancy, meaning how much work is active on the GPU.
一个寄存器分配决定就可能改变占用率，也就是 GPU 上同时运行的工作量。

37
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:04,705
That can change whether another scheduling decision helps.
这又会影响另一项调度决策是否奏效。

38
00:03:04,705 --> 00:03:08,268
The best settings depend on the workload.
最佳设置取决于具体任务。

39
00:03:08,268 --> 00:03:13,466
Ava: So how does Helion receive a chosen set of compiler controls?
Ava：Helion 怎么接收选好的编译器控制选项？

40
00:03:13,466 --> 00:03:19,678
Brian: Through an Advanced Control File, or ACF. It's a file applied at compile time.
Brian：通过高级控制文件（Advanced Control File，ACF），在编译时应用。

41
00:03:19,678 --> 00:03:28,072
Helion offers one setting to pin a chosen ACF and another to give its autotuner several ACFs to test.
Helion 提供一个选项来固定使用指定的 ACF，另一个选项让自动调优器测试多个 ACF。

42
00:03:28,072 --> 00:03:33,654
Ava: If I give it a list, could every file lose to the compiler's normal settings?
Ava：如果我提供一个列表，会不会所有文件都比不上编译器的默认设置？

43
00:03:33,654 --> 00:03:38,319
Brian: Absolutely. Helion adds a no-ACF candidate automatically.
Brian：完全可能。Helion 会自动加入一个不使用 ACF 的候选方案。

44
00:03:38,319 --> 00:03:43,067
That means the default compiler settings stay in the race.
这样，编译器的默认设置也会参与比较。

45
00:03:43,067 --> 00:03:48,164
The tuner selects an ACF only if its measured result wins.
只有实测结果胜出，调优器才会选择某个 ACF。

46
00:03:48,164 --> 00:03:52,209
Ava: Why test kernel settings and compiler settings together?
Ava：为什么要一起测试内核设置和编译器设置？

47
00:03:52,209 --> 00:03:56,242
Couldn't I finish one search, then start the other?
我不能先完成一轮搜索，再开始另一轮吗？

48
00:03:56,242 --> 00:03:59,856
Brian: You could, but you'd freeze the first choice too early.
Brian：可以，但这样会过早固定第一轮的选择。

49
00:03:59,856 --> 00:04:04,784
Imagine choosing a delivery route before learning which vehicle you'll use.
就像还不知道用什么车，就先选好送货路线。

50
00:04:04,784 --> 00:04:08,880
The best route for one vehicle might be poor for another.
适合一种车的最佳路线，换辆车可能就不合适了。

51
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:11,918
Ava: What's the GPU version of that problem?
Ava：这个问题在 GPU 上是怎样的？

52
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:17,508
Brian: Block size and pipeline stages affect register pressure and shared-memory use.
Brian：块大小和流水线阶段数会影响寄存器压力和共享内存用量。

53
00:04:17,508 --> 00:04:21,665
A compiler control can change how that pressure plays out.
编译器控制项会改变这些资源压力的影响。

54
00:04:21,665 --> 00:04:27,820
If you only test controls on one fixed block size, you may miss a better pairing.
如果只在固定的块大小下测试控制项，可能会错过更好的组合。

55
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:34,578
Ava: Right. So the joint search considers pairings that a two-step search might never see.
Ava：明白了。联合搜索能考虑到分两步搜索可能遗漏的组合。

56
00:04:34,578 --> 00:04:36,126
Brian: That's the key idea.
Brian：这就是关键。

57
00:04:36,126 --> 00:04:42,784
It doesn't promise the perfect answer, but it avoids that particular ordering problem.
它不保证找到最优解，但能避免这个搜索顺序带来的问题。

58
00:04:42,784 --> 00:04:49,328
The price is more trials: each extra ACF expands the compile-and-measure search.
代价是要测试更多配置：每增加一个 ACF，编译和测量的搜索范围就会扩大。

59
00:04:49,328 --> 00:04:55,126
Ava: Where do the ACFs come from? Do users need to learn every ptxas control?
Ava：这些 ACF 从哪里来？用户需要了解 ptxas 的每个控制项吗？

60
00:04:55,126 --> 00:04:59,440
Brian: Usually, no. NVIDIA's CompileIQ searches those controls.
Brian：通常不用。NVIDIA 的 CompileIQ 会搜索这些控制项。

61
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:12,348
It proposes candidate settings, compiles them, checks correctness against a reference, times the valid candidates, and carries strong candidates into later rounds.
它提出候选配置、编译并与参考结果核对正确性，再对正确的候选配置计时，把表现好的带入后续轮次。

62
00:05:12,348 --> 00:05:18,554
Ava: That sounds like an evolutionary search. What does a typical user start with?
Ava：听起来像进化搜索。一般用户从哪里入手？

63
00:05:18,554 --> 00:05:22,786
Brian: CompileIQ publishes pre-tuned catalogs called Booster Packs.
Brian：CompileIQ 发布了预先调优的配置集，叫作 Booster Packs。

64
00:05:22,786 --> 00:05:33,856
The article's Helion pack has twenty-four ACFs, tuned across Helion kernels and validated against ptxas from CUDA thirteen point four for B two hundred.
文章中的 Helion 配置包含 24 个 ACF，针对多个 Helion 内核调优，并用面向 B200 的 CUDA 13.4 版 ptxas 做了验证。

65
00:05:33,856 --> 00:05:38,934
Ava: Then I let Helion test that pack, and pin the winner for later runs?
Ava：那我让 Helion 测试这套配置，再把胜出的配置固定下来供以后运行？

66
00:05:38,934 --> 00:05:39,524
Brian: Exactly.
Brian：没错。

67
00:05:39,524 --> 00:05:47,197
If the pack doesn't cover your workload, the article also describes running a targeted CompileIQ search.
如果这套配置不适合你的工作负载，文章也介绍了如何运行有针对性的 CompileIQ 搜索。

68
00:05:47,197 --> 00:05:52,268
Either way, correctness checks matter before timing a candidate.
无论哪种方式，候选配置都要先检查正确性，再计时。

69
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:54,140
Ava: Let's get to the evidence.
Ava：来看看证据。

70
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:59,170
Did their main experiment actually perform the full joint search?
他们的主要实验真的做了完整的联合搜索吗？

71
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:06,526
Brian: The detailed case study fixes an existing Helion configuration and searches compiler controls beneath it.
Brian：详细案例固定了一个现有的 Helion 配置，然后搜索其底层的编译器控制项。

72
00:06:06,526 --> 00:06:08,487
That's a useful distinction.
这个区别值得注意。

73
00:06:08,487 --> 00:06:15,072
It tests whether the second layer has headroom even after Helion's first layer was tuned.
它检验的是：Helion 的第一层调优完成后，第二层是否还有提升空间。

74
00:06:15,072 --> 00:06:17,390
Ava: Which kernel did they use?
Ava：他们用了哪个内核？

75
00:06:17,390 --> 00:06:24,975
Brian: A pretuned NVFP4 decode kernel that multiplies packed weights by an activation vector and scales the output.
Brian：一个预先调优的 NVFP4 解码内核，它将打包权重乘以激活向量，再对输出进行缩放。

76
00:06:24,975 --> 00:06:30,100
It already had a checked-in configuration for the shape they tested.
针对测试的形状，它已有提交到代码库的配置。

77
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:32,202
Ava: And where was it measured?
Ava：在哪里测的？

78
00:06:32,202 --> 00:06:35,781
Brian: On a GB two hundred system with Blackwell hardware.
Brian：在采用 Blackwell 硬件的 GB200 系统上。

79
00:06:35,781 --> 00:06:44,413
This experiment used ptxas from CUDA thirteen point three, which differs from the Booster Pack's stated validation version.
这项实验使用 CUDA 13.3 版 ptxas，与 Booster Pack 标明的验证版本不同。

80
00:06:44,413 --> 00:06:47,360
They locked the GPU clock for timing.
他们锁定了 GPU 时钟频率进行计时。

81
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:51,694
Ava: What happened when CompileIQ optimized for runtime?
Ava：CompileIQ 以运行时间为目标优化后，结果怎样？

82
00:06:51,694 --> 00:07:01,913
Brian: Its search found an ACF that cut the measured time from about zero point zero nine seven one milliseconds to zero point zero nine two eight milliseconds.
Brian：搜索找到一个 ACF，将测得的运行时间从约 0.0971 毫秒降至 0.0928 毫秒。

83
00:07:01,913 --> 00:07:06,204
That's about four point seven percent faster in the search.
在搜索测量中，速度提高了约 4.7%。

84
00:07:06,204 --> 00:07:10,658
Ava: Search measurements can be lucky. Did they check again?
Ava：搜索测量可能碰巧偏好。他们重新验证了吗？

85
00:07:10,658 --> 00:07:10,943
Brian: Yes.
Brian：验证了。

86
00:07:10,943 --> 00:07:20,352
They independently remeasured the result twice, checked numerical output against a PyTorch reference, and applied statistical tests.
他们独立重复测量了两次，用 PyTorch 参考结果核对数值输出，并进行了统计检验。

87
00:07:20,352 --> 00:07:25,192
Both reruns showed a speedup of about four point eight percent.
两次复测都显示速度提高了约 4.8%。

88
00:07:25,192 --> 00:07:28,998
Ava: Could they aim the search at something other than runtime?
Ava：搜索目标可以不是运行时间吗？

89
00:07:28,998 --> 00:07:29,648
Brian: They did.
Brian：他们也试了。

90
00:07:29,648 --> 00:07:38,170
A profiler suggested the kernel was limited by registers, with achieved occupancy around twenty-one point six percent.
性能分析工具显示，该内核可能受寄存器限制，实际占用率约为 21.6%。

91
00:07:38,170 --> 00:07:45,092
It estimated possible headroom from occupancy, but that estimate wasn't a measured speedup.
它估算了提高占用率可能带来的提升空间，但那不是实测加速。

92
00:07:45,092 --> 00:07:48,634
Ava: So they searched for higher occupancy directly?
Ava：所以他们直接搜索更高的占用率？

93
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:55,183
Brian: Yes. The chosen ACF raised achieved occupancy by zero point one six percentage points.
Brian：对。选出的 ACF 将实际占用率提高了 0.16 个百分点。

94
00:07:55,183 --> 00:08:03,072
Independent timing then showed a smaller runtime gain, roughly one point seven five to two percent.
随后独立计时显示，运行时间的改善较小，约为 1.75% 至 2%。

95
00:08:03,072 --> 00:08:08,054
Ava: That's modest. What about optimizing two measures at once?
Ava：提升不算大。同时优化两个指标呢？

96
00:08:08,054 --> 00:08:11,952
Brian: CompileIQ can score candidates on multiple measures.
Brian：CompileIQ 可以根据多个指标给候选配置评分。

97
00:08:11,952 --> 00:08:15,550
They paired runtime with L1TEX cache throughput.
他们同时考察运行时间和 L1TEX 缓存吞吐量。

98
00:08:15,550 --> 00:08:24,220
The search looks for a Pareto frontier: candidates where improving one measure might require giving up another.
搜索会寻找帕累托前沿：在这些候选配置中，改善一个指标可能要牺牲另一个。

99
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:26,706
Ava: Did they have to make that trade?
Ava：他们需要做这种取舍吗？

100
00:08:26,706 --> 00:08:32,951
Brian: In this search, no. One candidate beat the other evaluated candidates on both measures.
Brian：这次不用。有一个候选配置在两个指标上都优于其他接受评估的配置。

101
00:08:32,951 --> 00:08:42,488
Fresh validation found a six point nine percent runtime speedup and a four point five percentage-point rise in L1TEX throughput.
新一轮验证发现，运行速度提升了 6.9%，L1TEX 吞吐率提高了 4.5 个百分点。

102
00:08:42,488 --> 00:08:47,974
Ava: I also saw two input shapes. Was that one ACF for both?
Ava：我还看到两种输入形状。它们用的是同一个 ACF 吗？

103
00:08:47,974 --> 00:08:51,677
Brian: Yes. They searched for a shared ACF across two shapes.
Brian：对。他们为两种形状搜索共用的 ACF。

104
00:08:51,677 --> 00:09:02,724
One candidate beat the default on both in independent validation: about five percent faster on the down-projection shape and about one percent on the other.
独立验证中，一个候选方案在两种形状上都优于默认配置：下投影形状快约 5%，另一种快约 1%。

105
00:09:02,724 --> 00:09:07,874
Ava: Does that mean an entire model gets six point nine percent faster?
Ava：这意味着整个模型会快 6.9% 吗？

106
00:09:07,874 --> 00:09:11,985
Brian: The article doesn't claim that. These are kernel results.
Brian：文章没有这么说。这些是内核的测试结果。

107
00:09:11,985 --> 00:09:17,898
For a model, you'd first profile which kernels dominate its work, then tune those.
对于模型，得先分析哪些内核占用时间最多，再针对它们调优。

108
00:09:17,898 --> 00:09:22,936
The model-level gain depends on how much time those kernels take.
整个模型能快多少，取决于这些内核占用多少时间。

109
00:09:22,936 --> 00:09:27,750
Ava: What would the practical workflow look like for someone using Helion today?
Ava：现在用 Helion 的人，实际该怎么做？

110
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:35,972
Brian: Pick a kernel that matters, search offline with matching ACFs, verify correctness and timing, then pin the winner.
Brian：选一个关键内核，用匹配的 ACF 离线搜索，验证正确性和耗时，然后固定表现最好的配置。

111
00:09:35,972 --> 00:09:42,092
The pinned file can travel with the kernel and be reapplied during later builds.
固定下来的配置文件可以随内核一起保存，在之后的构建中重新应用。

112
00:09:42,092 --> 00:09:47,290
Ava: You said matching ACFs. What's the risk if they don't match?
Ava：你说 ACF 要匹配。不匹配有什么风险？

113
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:50,888
Brian: ACFs are specific to hardware and toolkit versions.
Brian：ACF 与硬件和工具包版本有关。

114
00:09:50,888 --> 00:09:58,083
The article warns that using one for the wrong architecture can cause wrong results or runtime errors.
文章警告说，用在错误的架构上可能导致结果错误或运行时出错。

115
00:09:58,083 --> 00:10:01,608
It's more serious than losing a little speed.
这比损失一点速度严重得多。

116
00:10:01,608 --> 00:10:04,934
Ava: And the search itself sounds expensive.
Ava：而且搜索本身听起来很耗资源。

117
00:10:04,934 --> 00:10:05,654
Brian: It can be.
Brian：确实可能如此。

118
00:10:05,654 --> 00:10:12,926
Every ACF adds trials, and gains depend on the shape, workload, architecture, and remaining headroom.
每个 ACF 都会增加试验次数，收益则取决于形状、负载、架构和剩余的优化空间。

119
00:10:12,926 --> 00:10:17,524
The measured result on your own kernel is the one to trust.
最可信的，还是你在自己的内核上测得的结果。

120
00:10:17,524 --> 00:10:20,826
Ava: Give me the three-point recap before we go.
Ava：结束前，请用三点总结一下。

121
00:10:20,826 --> 00:10:24,355
Brian: First, Helion tunes the kernel's work plan.
Brian：第一，Helion 会调优内核的执行方案。

122
00:10:24,355 --> 00:10:32,481
Second, ACFs let it explore compiler choices underneath, and joint search can find useful pairings.
第二，ACF 让它探索底层编译器选项，联合搜索可能找到有效的组合。

123
00:10:32,481 --> 00:10:38,576
Third, validate on your target hardware, then pin the measured winner.
第三，在目标硬件上验证，再固定实测表现最好的配置。

124
00:10:38,576 --> 00:10:41,890
Ava: A few percent can hide below a well-tuned kernel.
Ava：即使内核已经调得很好，底下也可能还藏着几个百分点的提升空间。

125
00:10:41,890 --> 00:10:45,622
Thanks for listening, and we'll see you next time.
感谢收听，我们下期再见。
